hadiths[10]{hadithnumber,text}:
"504","Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Sallam narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Wuhayb. I heard Kharijah ibn Zayd say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the most dignified of people in his sitting; he would hardly extend anything of his limbs."
"505","Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from al-Awza'i, from Urwah ibn Ruwaym, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing my Lord forbade me after the worship of idols was drinking wine and quarreling with men."
"506","Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Abthar narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Abu al-Safar, from Ali ibn Rabi'ah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Mecca, he set out at once for Ta'if, with Abu Bakr with him, and with him the two sons of Sa'id ibn al-As. Abu Bakr said: Whose grave is this? They said: The grave of Sa'id ibn al-As. Abu Bakr said: May Allah curse the occupant of this grave, for he used to oppose Allah and His Messenger. The two sons of Sa'id said: May Allah curse Abu Quhafah, for he would neither honor the guest nor ward off disgrace. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Reviling the dead angers the living; so when you revile the polytheists, revile them all together."
"507","al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: A man came to al-Abbas and said: What of al-Ghaytalah, the soothsayer of Banu Sahm, in the Fire with Abd al-Muttalib? So al-Abbas struck his nose. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is with one of you that he hurts his brother in a matter even if it is true?"
"508","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Yahya, meaning Ibn Sa'id, narrated to us, from Ali ibn Husayn, that Abdullah ibn Ubayy said: If we return to Medina, the mightier will surely expel the lowlier from it; that was on the expedition of Tabuk. He said: And the last of the people had not yet alighted. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: March on, march on. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not command a man of his people to strike his neck? He said: I dislike that one should be angered thereby whom I do not wish to anger."
"509","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Mahri narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah informed me, from al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Hadrami, raising the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Straighten your circles, for when the angels come to sit and find crookedness in them, they turn back."
"510","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Tariq, from al-Sha'bi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a noble man of a people comes to you, honor him. Abu Dawud said: It has been narrated with a connected chain, but it is nothing."
"511","Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd, meaning Ibn Ibrahim, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When there are two, the third shall not approach them until he seeks their permission."
"512","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Abd al-A'la ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwah informed me, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, who said: I heard that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man is not separated from his father. I was sitting with an uncle of mine when he came, and we made room for him between us. Abd al-A'la said: This is but my uncle. He said: Yes; the paternal uncle is a father in the Book of Allah."
"513","Abu Salih al-Antaki narrated to us, Abu Ishaq informed us, from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not seize anyone on mere accusation, nor believe anyone against anyone."
